<title>USA: Castle Rock sees merger leading to job cuts.</title>
<headline>Castle Rock sees merger leading to job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Castle Rock Entertainment on Monday said it planned to cut jobs as a result of the merger earlier this year with Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>According to the newspaper Variety, as many as 80 of Castle Rock's 130 employees could lose their jobs. A spokeswoman for the company confirmed that Castle Rock would make some cuts but said a final decision on the number had not yet been made.</p>
<p>She said the layoffs would occur in areas where Time Warner and Castle Rock have duplicative operations, including marketing, physical production and international distribution.</p>
<p>Castle Rock was part of Turner Broadcasting before Turner's merger with Time Warner.</p>
